    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.align\n\n### Description\n\nIt would be nice if `mini.align`'s `ga` and `gA` maps accepted an optional count that was interpreted as the number of lines to operate on.\r\n\r\nFor example, in order to `=`-align the 5 lines counting from the current one, currently this is done via `ga4j=`. I am proposing to also allow `5ga=`. Note this saves a keystroke.",
