    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis indeed sounds interesting. Yet I don't think it is enough to justify added complexity (both in code and mental). Right now `ga` and `gA` are regular operators (same as built-in `d`, `c`, etc.) and always expect textobject/motion after it. Having a different fixed linewise behavior for when `v:count` is supplied seems to be going against all established operators logic.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
